    "5-year-old boy without personal or family immunodeficiency history had 29 months of intermittent fever, recurrent diarrhea, and hematochezia after earlier EBV infection with hepatomegaly.",
    "The active course included recurrent fever, abdominal pain, diarrhea, two weeks of GI hemorrhage, duodenal ulcer bleeding, hypovolemic shock, polyuria, convulsions, severe hyponatremia, hepatosplenomegaly, anemia, thrombocytopenia, coagulopathy, and high procalcitonin during acute deterioration.",
    "Admission labs included WBC 6.02 x10^9/L, hemoglobin 112 g/L, platelets 75 x10^9/L, D-dimer 3.82 mg/L, aPTT 36.4 s, fibrinogen 1.66 g/L, albumin 26 g/L, triglycerides 1.58 mmol/L, and ferritin 227.5 ug/L.",
